                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "57144775",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198061190773",
                            "num_reviews": 21,
                            "playtime_forever": 16,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 16,
                            "last_played": 1573608780
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Now before you're put off by this game because it's made by the killer keem and his team - I'd like people to give it a chance. \n\n$5 is the asking price so let's keep this in mind of a small development team. \n\nThe gameplay is easy to understand and controls are well explained throughout the levels, Some levels are a good level of simple and challenging as they go through the stages or \"Chapters\" of this game. The gnome recruitment is a brilliant feature which I think gives the game it's stand out selling point. \n\nWhilst the game is well built, I wouldn't say it is nearly polished enough for people to pay anymore than $5 - but the point is that this is fun, yes it has a few bugs and if you have a widescreen monitor, the text cuts of sometimes, but it's a great little hack and slash level up-er of a game and I think if you've got a spare $5 it's really not quite the disappointment I think a lot of people were expecting. \n\n7/10  - Great game-play, fantastic mechanics to make it unique, a few bugs and isn't quite graphically polished either, but nonetheless great fun. \n",
